From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiron Builder <builder@chiron.local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:45:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/44] arm64: dts: add the Chiron board description

Chiron is a Yandex A311D2/T7C appliance. The board file includes the locked
SoC dtsi and describes only what this board has: eMMC, the W2 SDIO Wi-Fi with
its power regulator, the MIPI panel and its backlight, and the DRM topology
that drives that panel. Another board dts is never included: the VIM4N file
enables an SD controller whose pins are this board Wi-Fi host wake and power
enable.

Every value is carried over from the hardware-accepted Chiron device
tree, including the reserved-memory layout. codec_mm_cma matters beyond
codecs: the display allocates its scanout buffer from the heap-codecmm
dma-heap, which is backed by that pool and must be physically contiguous.

The panel description is split out because it is long: three HX83102E panels
with identical timing and different init sequences, selected by panel_type on
the command line.

(cherry picked from commit 4c7dbac6983a90d4b8fffdc253a03ec6418998ca)
